# Layout and starting the agent

Read this before cloning, before choosing the folder to start the agent in, and when investigating "the agent did not see a rule".

## Layout

```text
{{ project_slug }}/        meta-repository git, branch main
├── AGENTS.md             agent rules
├── repos.toml            repository registry, the only list of clones
├── openspec/             OpenSpec and sdd-kit: specs, changes, protocols (after mise run kit:install)
│   └── clones            clone list for sdd-kit, generated from repos.toml
├── docs/                 agent rules, decisions, clone backlog
├── ast-grep/             shared rules for clone code
├── mise-tasks/           mise tasks, one folder per clone
├── scripts/              registry script and task helpers
├── tests/                meta-repository tests
└── repos/                in .gitignore
    └── <name>/           own git, on its rest branch
```

The meta-repository and the clones are separate git repositories. `git status` in the root shows no changes in `repos/`, and a commit in the root does not include clone files. So git runs inside the folder of the repository the task touches.

## Where to start the agent

Always from the meta-repository root, also for a task in a single clone. The reasons:

- Claude Code reads `AGENTS.md` in the start folder and every folder above it, and loads subfolder rules when the agent opens a file in that subfolder. From the root, the meta-repository's `AGENTS.md` is there from the first step, and a clone's `CLAUDE.md` appears when the agent opens a file in that clone. That is why `AGENTS.md` explicitly requires reading the clone's rules before an edit.
- `.claude/settings.json` and hooks are taken only from the start folder. The sdd-kit hooks and the `agent-git-guard` hook work only when started from the root.
- sdd-kit in meta-repository mode sees the tests in the clones, checks their scenario markers, and forbids changing `openspec/` inside a clone from the root (`openspec/protocols/metarepo.md`).

A session started inside a clone sees the meta-repository's `AGENTS.md` but not its settings and hooks. Use that only for small edits without OpenSpec.

## Cloning

`mise run clone` creates the clones. The list is `repos.toml`; `mise run repos:sync` writes it into `[bootstrap.repos]` in `mise.toml`, which `mise run clone` reads, and into `openspec/clones` for sdd-kit. Details in [../../repos/README.md](../../repos/README.md), the reason for the choice in [ADR 0001](../adr/0001-clones-via-mise-bootstrap-repos.md). A new clone is added with `mise run add-repo`; `mise run check` fails while the lists disagree.

## Other people's changes

A clone may contain changes by another person or another agent session. Before an edit, run `mise run status` and look at `CHANGED`. Do not run `git add .` in a clone; add files by name.
